From 675cc43bcdcd7cdd7ab6d34ed9fbbfb6ff33a6e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Denton <z@chdenton.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:30:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom] Check VOPD register banks by operand cache

FMAMK encodes its addend in VSRC1 but reads it through SRC2, whose bank mask is 1 rather than 3. Comparing encoded fields admitted illegal FMAMK pairs and missed conflicts between FMAMK addends and tied FMAC accumulators.

Describe the register feeding each operand cache in the component tables and use that mapping in both placement relations and native packet legality. Preserve legal dual operations, including pairs whose encoded VSRC1 operands use different caches, and report SRC2 bank conflicts explicitly.

Add placement, assembly, and diagnostic regressions. Four assembly cases fail before the fix and pass afterward. Validation: 17 generator tests, 16 native/schedule fixture suites, and 15 downstream GPU kernel tests. The previously failing BF16 GELU family now matches all 4160 baseline outputs bitwise; LLVM accepts its emitted VOPD instructions.
